          %title
          %p
            %strong Alexander (or Sasha) Beĭlinson
            is currently a professor at University of Chicago. He was student of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Yuri Manin
            at Moscow State University, with main works in algebraic geometry. He has made visionary contributions to the study of algebraic cycles, automorphic forms and L-functions,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motive"} motive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfeld"} Vladimir Drinfel'd
            are of large importance to mathematical physics, especially on their concept of
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+algebra"}> chiral algebra
              s
            which are an approach to a chiral part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            on a curve, which is a geometric counterpart of the theory of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebra"} vertex operator algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands"} geometric Langlands
            program, which has been continued in his collaboration with Drinfel’d and also by Ed Frenkel, Dennis Gaitsgory,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivan+Mirkovi%C4%87"} Ivan Mirković
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Witten
          %p
            Beĭlinson has substantial contributions to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+representation+theory"} geometric representation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Be%C4%ADlinson-Bernstein+localization"} Beĭlinson-Bernstein localization
            theorem, which lead to influx of the algebraic methods involving algebraic D-modules to representation theory. With Kazhdan, Beĭlinson has used D-modules in the proof of Jantzen’s conjecture, where he introduced the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-affinity"} D-affinity
            and the geometric viewpoint via D-schemes. In the work on Hitchin fibration and Hitchin integrable system (with Drinfel’d) much of technique of algebraic geometry on ind-schemes, including study of D-modules is developed and used. In similar spirit to D-modules, he was also using perverse modules; with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Gabber"} Ofer Gabber
            %strong decomposition theorem
            (see a survey:
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bull/2009-46-04/S0273-0979-09-01260-9/S0273-0979-09-01260-9.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Beĭlinson has shown a remarkable structure of the bounded derived category of coherent sheaves on projective spaces, and its connections to quivers. This work, together with subsequent work with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Bernstein"} Joseph Bernstein
            and also later works of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"} Mikhail Kapranov
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Bondal"} Alexei Bondal
            marked the birth of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} derived noncommutative algebraic geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ginzburg"} Victor Ginzburg
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Manin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Soergel"} Wolfgang Soergel
            and others, Beĭlinson introduced a wide picture of “Koszul duality patterns” in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
          %p
            His other works concentrated on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives"} motives
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+regulators"} higher regulators
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                epsilon-factors
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/epsilon-factors"} ?
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands.html"} geometric Langlands homepage
            %li
              %p
                wikipedia:
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Beilinson"} Alexander Beilinson
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Introducing the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perverse+sheaves"} perverse sheaves
            (and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/t-structures"} t-structures
            on
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Bernstein"} Joseph Bernstein
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"} Pierre Deligne
              = succeed "," do
                %em Faisceaux pervers
              %strong 100
              (1982) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://smf.emath.fr/publications/faisceaux-pervers"}> ISBN:978-2-85629-878-7
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/Faisceaux%20pervers.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=751966"} MR86g:32015
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Beilinson85
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"} Alexander Beilinson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher regulators and values of L-functions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=intd&paperid=73&option_lang=eng"} mathnet (Russian)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007%2FBF02105861"} DOI
            %li#Beilinson80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher regulators of curves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=faa&paperid=1800&option_lang=eng"} mathnet (Russian)
            %li#Beilinson87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Height pairing between algebraic cycles
                = succeed "," do
                  %em K-Theory, Arithmetic and Geometry
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0078364"} DOI
            %li
              %p
                A. Beilinson, J. Bernstein,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Localisations de
                    = succeed "\u2013modules" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝔤
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                %strong 292
                (1981), 15–18.
            %li
              %p
                A. A. Beilinson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V.+Drinfeld"} V. Drinfeld
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chiral+Algebras"} Chiral Algebras
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands.html"} here
            %li
              %p
                A. A. Beilinson, V. Ginzburg, W. Soergel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Koszul duality patterns in representation theory
                %strong 9
                (2): 473–527 (1996).
            %li
              %p
                A. A. Beĭlinson, V. A. Ginsburg, V. V. Schechtman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Koszul duality
                %strong 5
                (1988), no. 3, 317–350.
            %li
              %p
                A. Beilinson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ginzburg"} V. Ginzburg
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing"} Wall-crossing
                    functors and
                    = succeed "-modules" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %strong 3
                (electronic), 1–31 (1999)
            %li
              %p
                A. Beĭlinson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Bernstein"} J. Bernstein
                = succeed "," do
